The handler is `unfavorite` in `src/app/features/favorite/controllers.rs`, lines 21–32.

```rust
pub async fn unfavorite(
    state: web::Data<AppState>,
    req: HttpRequest,
    path: web::Path<ArticleIdSlug>,
) -> ApiResponse {
    let current_user = auth::get_current_user(&req)?;
    let article_title_slug = path.into_inner();
    state
        .di_container
        .favorite_usecase
        .unfavorite_article(current_user, article_title_slug)
}
```

It is registered in `src/app/drivers/routes.rs` (lines 54–63). The `/favorite` scope has `post()` mapped to `favorite` and `delete()` mapped to `unfavorite`, so `DELETE /api/articles/{slug}/favorite` reaches this function. The handler takes the current user from the request, then calls `FavoriteUsecase::unfavorite_article`, which uses the favorite repository.
